# /etc/default/prometheus
#
# Consumed by the prometheus systemd unit via EnvironmentFile=, whose
# ExecStart is literally `/usr/bin/prometheus $ARGS`. Every setting
# below is a process flag with no equivalent in prometheus.yml, so a
# server rebuilt from this repo without this file comes up looking
# healthy while quietly missing all of it.
#
#   --storage.tsdb.retention.size=20GB
#       The only size cap that exists. global.retention in the YAML
#       is time-based and does not bound disk.
#
#   --web.listen-address=127.0.0.1:9092
#   --web.route-prefix=/
#       Prometheus serves on 9092 behind nginx, which owns 9090 and
#       fronts it at /prometheus. route-prefix stays / so the app
#       still answers a bare /metrics; see the prometheus job in
#       prometheus.yml, which scrapes this listener directly rather
#       than going through nginx (that vhost requires auth and would
#       return 401).
#
#   --web.external-url=...
#       What Prometheus puts in generated links and alert URLs. Wrong
#       or absent, the UI works but every link it emits is unusable
#       from outside the box.
#
#   --web.enable-remote-write-receiver
#       The load-bearing one. This box is a remote-write sink for
#       external clusters, and that traffic is the bulk of the TSDB
#       (~183k series against ~10k scraped locally). Nothing in
#       prometheus.yml references it, so losing this flag drops all
#       of it with no config diff to explain why.

ARGS="--storage.tsdb.retention.size=20GB --web.listen-address=127.0.0.1:9092 --web.enable-remote-write-receiver --web.external-url=https://snoc-beelink.fold-leaffish.ts.net/prometheus --web.route-prefix=/"
